uire making incidental discussion a chapter. Preserve heading context, historical/conditional scope, adjacent prerequisites and corrections. An indivisible mixed candidate retains its real project content and attributes its external examples; never discard it wholesale. sourceRouting preserves excerpt-level membership even inside shared original messages. References keep their own subjects and only the evidenced implication for this project. One-off developer requests remain scoped requirements or history, never permanent product features or prohibitions. PROJECT SCOPE ROUTING v4: In this SAME response review EVERY candidate against projectBoundary, reading lead, scopeDetails and literal scopeQuotes together. scopeContext reports omissions; absent context proves nothing and cannot earn completed review. Return required scope:[{id,kind,reason,quote}], or scope:[] when no candidates need flags. Unlisted candidates are project content only after semantic review.
